+++ b/skills/trailer-maker/SKILL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+---
+name: trailer-maker
+description: Makes a game trailer from a Unity project: beat sheet, captured gameplay clips and title cards, an audio bed (music, VO, SFX via the ElevenLabs tools or a licensed track), an edit list rendered with ffmpeg by scripts/render_edit.py, then a review by three reviewers before it ships. Use when asked for a trailer, teaser, gameplay reel, store video, launch or announcement video, or to re-cut one.
+---
+
+# trailer-maker
+
+Make a 30–90 s trailer whose every cut is planned, rendered from an edit list, and reviewed. `T` = the trailer folder, `Trailer/<name>/` in the project (not under `Assets/`). `<skills>` = the folder holding these skills.
+
+## Setup
+
+- ffmpeg: `python3 <skills>/trailer-maker/scripts/render_edit.py caps` (needs `libx264` and `aac`). Title cards are made
+in Unity (with your game's font), so the slim Homebrew formula is enough; `ffmpeg-full` adds `drawtext`/libass if
+you want burned-in captions. `TRAILER_FFMPEG` picks a specific build.
+- ElevenLabs tools (`music`, `tts`, `sound_effect`) need a key on the ElevenLabs page; music needs a paid plan.
+
+## Workflow
+
+1. **Beat sheet** → `T/BEATS.md`: hook (first 3 s), the core loop, escalation, the money shot, title, call to action
+   (store / wishlist / date). One row per beat: seconds, what's on screen, audio cue. Ask the user to approve it.
+2. **Capture** each beat in Play Mode (Unity Recorder, 1080p or 4K, 60 fps) to `T/clips/`; title and end cards
+   as PNGs from a Unity scene to `T/cards/`. The Recorder movie may not **capture its audio**: record game audio separately or rebuild it in the mix (references/audio.md).
+3. **Audio bed**: music via `music` with a `composition_plan` whose
+sections match the beat sheet, VO via `tts`, SFX via `sound_effect`; copy files to `T/audio/`, record items in
+   `T/audio/sources.json` (references/audio.md).
+4. **Edit list** → `T/edit.json` (format in the script's header): cuts land on the music's section changes.
+   `render_edit.py check T/edit.json` until `RESULT: OK`.
+5. **Render**: `render_edit.py render T/edit.json` → `T/out/trailer.mp4`. The file is indexed as an item, so the
+   user can play it from the chat.
+6. **Review** with the three reviewers (references/reviewers.md); fix and re-render until none fails, at most 3 rounds.
+7. **Report** → `T/REPORT.md`: length, beats, sources and licenses, credits spent, reviewer scores, open issues.
+
+## Rules
+
+- Never regenerate audio that already fits: reuse items (`sources.json`). Each generation is billed.
+- Footage is real gameplay from the current build; no mock-ups presented as gameplay.
+- Keep `T/edit.json` the source of truth: a change is an edit-list change and a re-render, never a hand-edited export.
