@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# Trailer reviewers
+
+Three reviewer subagents look at the render independently (frames every 0.5 s, e.g.
+`ffmpeg -i T/out/trailer.mp4 -vf fps=2 T/review/f_%03d.png`, plus `T/BEATS.md`, `T/edit.json` and the loudness
+summary). Each scores 1–5 and lists concrete fixes as edit-list changes. The lowest score counts: below 3 fails.
+
+| Reviewer | Asks |
+|---|---|
+| **Hook Critic** (a player scrolling a store page) | Is the game's genre and fantasy clear in 3 s? Would I keep watching at 10 s? Is the call to action readable and long enough (≥ 2 s)? |
+| **Editor** (pacing and craft) | Do cuts land on the music's section changes? Any shot shorter than 0.5 s or longer than 4 s without a reason? Black frames, letterboxing, jumps, UI clutter, debug overlays? |
+| **Sound Mixer** (audio) | Is VO intelligible over music? Loudness near −14 LUFS, no clipping? Does every big on-screen hit have a sound? Is the end clean (no cut-off tail)? |
+
+Write each review to `T/review/<reviewer>.md` and the scores to `T/REPORT.md`. At most 3 rounds; after that the
+user decides with the open issues listed.
